kubectl api-resources

it will list all the resources

The kubectl api-resources command prints a complete list of all supported resource types available on your Kubernetes cluster's API server. It helps you check exact resource names, short aliases, API groups, and whether a resource is bound to a specific namespace.

Output Columns Explained

Running kubectl api-resources displays five columns of information:
• NAME: The plural name of the resource used in commands (such as pods or deployments).
• SHORTNAMES: Common abbreviations you can type to save time (such as po for pods or svc for services).
• APIVERSION: The API group and version required in the apiVersion field of your YAML manifests (such as v1 or apps/v1).
• NAMESPACED: Shows true if the resource lives inside a namespace, or false if it applies across the entire cluster (like nodes).
• KIND: The exact capitalized name used in the kind field of your YAML manifests (such as Pod or Deployment).

