once you got resource types, you can use explain command to understand the resource
kubectl explain <object_type>

The kubectl explain command prints the official API documentation for any Kubernetes resource and its configuration fields directly in your terminal. It pulls schema details straight from your cluster's OpenAPI specification, showing field descriptions, expected data types, and whether a field is required.

You can use dot notation to drill down from a top-level resource into deeply nested YAML fields:
• Inspect a top-level resource: Run kubectl explain pod to view the overview, API version, and top-level fields (apiVersion, kind, metadata, spec, status) of a Pod.
• Drill into nested fields: Run kubectl explain pod.spec.containers to see all available settings for a container, such as image, ports, and resources.
• Check a specific property: Run kubectl explain deployment.spec.replicas to verify its exact data type (such as integer) and default behavior.

kubectl explain pod
kubectl explain pods.spec
kubectl explain pods --resursive
